@id=areas-for-reading-epics-for-work @kind=decision
Feature: Features are filed by area; an epic names its work and goes once it is built

  Not durable epics or packs, which outlive their work and come to gather all of it, nor an area tag,
  which repeats a folder: a feature lives in the folder of its area, which readers browse and
  CODEOWNERS routes, and an epic names the work toward one outcome with `@includes:` — beside that
  work, in a folder of its own, when it is one area's, and in the plan when it spans areas. The price
  is that sdp reads no meaning into an area or an epic's folder, and that an epic is kept true and deleted
  by hand, its features then joining their area.
